## Why This Is Asked
Tests a runtime-pluggable policy architecture and safe, per-namespace swapping without restart.

## Key Concepts
- Strategy pattern: EvictionPolicy interface
- Registry for plugin policies
- Per-namespace binding and hot-swapping
- Thread-safety and observability

## Code Example
```typescript
interface EvictionPolicy {
  onPut(key: any, now?: number): void
  onAccess(key: any, now?: number): void
  evict(entries: Map<any, any>): any | undefined
}
class LRU implements EvictionPolicy { /* ... */ }
class LFU implements EvictionPolicy { /* ... */ }
class TTL implements EvictionPolicy { /* ... */ }
// Registration
class PolicyRegistry {
  private static registry = new Map<string, () => EvictionPolicy>();
  static register(name: string, factory: () => EvictionPolicy) { this.registry.set(name, factory) }
  static getFactory(name: string): (() => EvictionPolicy) | undefined { return this.registry.get(name) }
}
// Usage
const namespace = 'users:cache';
const policyFactory = PolicyRegistry.getFactory('timeAwareLFU');
if (policyFactory) cache.setPolicy(namespace, policyFactory());
```

